sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Owner web / CLI
  participant MM as Media Management
  participant M as media_db
  participant P as Processing API
  participant D as processing_db
  participant Q as Redis / RQ
  participant W as P worker
  participant S as Source bucket
  participant O as Output bucket

  Note over C,O: PROPOSED — designed, not implemented. HTTP calls are synchronous; RQ work is asynchronous. Public /jobs ID means asset_id.
  C->>MM: /auth login; existing HTTPS cookie session
  MM-->>C: Session cookie (CLI keeps cookie jar)
  C->>MM: POST /upload with cookie + video + stable Idempotency-Key
  MM->>MM: Verify owner, video type and measured size <= 100 MiB
  MM->>S: Store source using MM source credentials
  MM->>M: Commit Asset + source descriptor + pending intent + request key
  M-->>MM: Durable intake confirmed
  MM->>S: ReadSource GET grant (15-minute design default)
  MM->>P: SubmitJob(asset_id, owner_id, source, operations, source_url, expiry) + token + X-Owner-Id
  P->>D: Lock owner-bound asset guard; commit Job + queued Attempt or return existing
  D-->>P: Durable internal Job UUID + state
  P->>Q: Enqueue job_id + attempt_id after DB commit
  Note over P,Q: Queue gaps belong to P reconciliation; Redis is not Job truth.
  alt Submit acknowledgement received
    P-->>MM: Job UUID + queued state
    MM->>M: Record internal correlation + submitted state; clear pending
  else Acknowledgement lost after commit; idempotent transport retry
    Note over MM,M: Durable pending intent survives; MM resubmits it.
    MM->>S: Mint fresh source_url for same revision
    MM->>P: Repeat SubmitJob(same asset/owner/revision/request, new URL)
    P->>D: Find same fingerprint; URL and expiry excluded
    D-->>P: Existing Job UUID and current state
    P-->>MM: Existing Job; no new job or retry attempt
    MM->>M: Reconcile correlation + submitted state; clear pending
  end
  MM-->>C: 202 accepted; public reference = asset_id
  Note over MM,M: P outage: durable upload still 202; pending status reads are 200 queued/pending with no outputs.

  Q-->>W: Asynchronous RQ delivery of job_id + reserved attempt_id
  W->>D: Claim current reserved queued Attempt; never create at claim
  D-->>W: Claim + job/owner/asset/revision
  alt Submit source_url is expired or refresh is needed
    W->>W: Validate its live Attempt locally
    W->>MM: POST /internal/v1/assets/{asset_id}/source-access; reverse token + X-Owner-Id + revision
    MM->>M: Check own Asset owner, immutable revision, not-deleted
    M-->>MM: Source authorised
    Note over MM,P: MM does not call P or read processing_db to validate attempts.
    MM->>S: ReadSource: fresh single-object GET, 15-minute default
    MM-->>W: source_url + expires_at + immutable descriptor
  else Submit URL remains usable
    W->>W: Use temporary source_url; never source credentials
  end
  W->>S: Download using presigned GET
  S-->>W: Source bytes
  W->>W: Standard MP4 + best-effort HLS; MKV/MP3 are edit-only compatibility
  W->>O: Write job/attempt-specific output objects; output-write credentials only
  W->>D: Conditional winning-attempt completion; publish durable refs
  D-->>W: Done + MP4 ref + optional HLS ref

  loop Owner polls through same entrypoint
    C->>MM: GET /jobs/{asset_id} + cookie
    MM->>M: Owner + live Asset lookup; internal correlation
    MM->>P: Owner-scoped GetJob + MM service token
    P->>D: Filter by stored owner and Job UUID
    D-->>P: State + durable output refs
    P-->>MM: Observed Job result (no playback URL)
    MM->>M: Compose public response from live P result; no required stored cache
    MM->>O: Sign 15-minute primary output GET with output-read/sign role
    MM-->>C: Live owner status + primary output URL + MM HLS route if available
  end
  C->>O: Temporary signed primary-output GET
  O-->>C: Primary-output bytes
  opt HLS available — playlists remain on owner-authorised MM routes
    C->>MM: GET /jobs/{asset_id}/hls/master.m3u8 + cookie
    MM->>M: Owner Asset + live P output prefix; validate HLS path
    MM->>O: Read playlist using output-read role
    O-->>MM: Playlist bytes
    MM-->>C: Playlist body; private no-store; relative URIs stay on MM
    C->>MM: Rendition playlist via same owner route
    MM-->>C: Authorised playlist body
    C->>MM: Segment via same owner route
    MM->>MM: Recheck owner + safe path; sign segment
    MM-->>C: 307 fresh signed segment URL
    C->>O: Signed segment GET
    O-->>C: Segment bytes
  end
  Note over C,O: Durable refs stay in P. Submitted P outage/missing Job: 503. Retry reserves one queued Attempt by retry_request_id; Submit replay creates none.
